From e570e579bedab6ad622a825f77491c6b53ffe8ee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tim Besard <tim.besard@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 2 Jul 2026 13:56:01 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] core-math: handle FP16 powr indeterminate forms

powr is implemented on top of the half `pow` builtin, which returns 1 for the
indeterminate forms 1^inf, 0^0 and inf^0. powr must instead return NaN for all
three (OpenCL powr special values). Add the three overrides between the x<0 and
the NaN-propagation checks; the vector overloads inherit the fix through
DEFINE_FP16_EXPR_V_VV.

This fixes the CTS math_brute_force powr fp16 failure reported when building
with FP16 forced on under ENABLE_CONFORMANCE (powr(1, inf) returned 1 instead
of NaN).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit ed1a18051784e7f7351d13eb50d475dc97cc10c6)
---
 lib/kernel/core-math/promotedf16.cl | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/lib/kernel/core-math/promotedf16.cl b/lib/kernel/core-math/promotedf16.cl
index 9a275303e..c03e39316 100644
--- a/lib/kernel/core-math/promotedf16.cl
+++ b/lib/kernel/core-math/promotedf16.cl
@@ -248,6 +248,11 @@ powr (half x, half y)
   x = (xu == (ushort)0x8000) ? (half)0 : x;       /* -0 -> +0 */
   half r = pow (x, y);
   r = (xu > (ushort)0x8000) ? (half)NAN : r;       /* x < 0 -> NaN */
+  /* pow() returns 1 for the indeterminate forms, but powr() must return NaN:
+     powr(1, +-inf), powr(+-0, +-0) and powr(+inf, +-0) are all NaN. */
+  r = (x == (half)1 && isinf (y)) ? (half)NAN : r;       /* 1^inf   */
+  r = (x == (half)0 && y == (half)0) ? (half)NAN : r;    /* 0^0     */
+  r = (isinf (x) && y == (half)0) ? (half)NAN : r;       /* inf^0   */
   r = isnan (x) ? (half)NAN : r;
   r = isnan (y) ? (half)NAN : r;
   return r;
